        "v": 5,
        "title": "Rename dynamic agent template fields for clarity",
        "summary": "DynamicAgentConfig schema refactors field names: `name` to `displayName`, `purpose` to `parentPrompt`, `promptSchema` to `inputSchema`, `userInputPrompt` to `instructionsPrompt`, `agentStepPrompt` to `stepPrompt`, and `spawnableAgents` to `subagents`. Updates in `backend/src/templates/agent-registry.ts`, `run-agent-step.ts`, and templates ensure consistent naming across the agent system. Breaking change for custom agent templates; migrate field names in `.agents/templates/*.ts` and override JSONs.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T12:11:30.034Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The system renamed the labels it uses for custom agent templates, the field called 'name' is now 'display name', 'purpose' is now 'parent prompt', and 'spawnable agents' is now 'sub-agents', along with a few other similar changes. This matters only to people who have written their own agent templates; if you have, your templates will stop working until you update them by replacing the old label names with the new ones. If you just use the built-in agents and haven't touched the templates yourself, you won't see any difference. The change is live today.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "bc8bca8613af",
