        "at": "2026-09-14T23:09:22.056Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If you updated to the latest version today, you'll get a handful of small improvements that were folded into this release. One notable change renamed several settings inside the agent-template system to clearer names (for example, the label that used to be called 'name' is now 'displayName', and 'purpose' is now 'parentPrompt'), which mainly helps people who build custom agent templates. The release also adds an 'autocompleted' flag to the data sent about tool calls, and makes the optional system prompt plus a new user-input prompt available when configuring agents. There are no visible buttons or menus you would click for most people, but if you author agent templates, you'll notice the field names have changed and the template now supports an extra prompt you can set for each conversation turn. Behind the scenes, this release is simply the version label being bumped; the user-facing changes listed above are what you actually receive when you move to this version.",
