        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Print mode JSON streaming support",
        "summary": "Core streaming pipeline now emits structured `PrintModeObject` chunks alongside plain text via `onResponseChunk`. `tool-executor.ts` injects `tool_call` objects into the stream, while `spawn-agents` handlers filter non-string chunks to prevent subagent stream corruption. Covers `backend` execution loop, `common` type definitions, and `npm-app` display overrides. Migration requires consumers to handle `string | PrintModeObject` union types.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T12:03:06.255Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If you watched the assistant work, you would now see it occasionally stream extra, structured bits of information alongside its regular text replies. These structured bits are non-language data the system uses to coordinate actions, and a few specific places in the flow intentionally skip over them so the main conversation stays as plain text. The change is live today and only affects how the assistant communicates with itself and the display layer, not the visible chat you see.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
